+ <div class="doc">
+   <p class="eyebrow">Reference · August 2026</p>
+   <h1>How Forge Works</h1>
+   <p class="dek">Forge is a design system stored as definitions and operated through tools. You describe <em>things</em> (objects) as bundles of <em>capabilities</em> (traits); Forge assembles them into screens per <em>context</em>, styles them with <em>tokens</em> under a <em>brand</em>, and exports screens, code, charts and theme files — checking its own output as it goes. This page explains each piece, what it actually contains, and what you can do with it.</p>
+
+   <nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents">
+     <ol>
+       <li><a href="#overview">The pieces, in one picture</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#traits">Traits — what one is, what it contains</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#trait-inventory">The trait inventory (41)</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#objects">Objects and composition</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#object-inventory">The object inventory (11)</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#contexts">Contexts, regions and components</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#tokens">Tokens, themes and brands</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#generate">Generating screens and code</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#charts">Charts and dashboards</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#certify">Certification and checks</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#operate">Operating it: starting, connecting, tools</a></li>
+       <li><a href="#extend">Extending it — and what it does not do</a></li>
+     </ol>
+   </nav>
+
+   <!-- 1 -->
+   <h2 id="overview"><span class="n">01</span>The pieces, in one picture</h2>
+   <div class="flow" role="list">
+     <div role="listitem"><i>define</i><b>Traits</b>Reusable capabilities: fields + settings + UI pieces per screen + tokens.</div>
+     <div role="listitem"><i>define</i><b>Objects</b>Things you model (User, Product, Invoice…) = a list of traits + a few own fields.</div>
+     <div role="listitem"><i>assemble</i><b>Contexts</b>List, detail, form, timeline, card, inline (+ chart, dashboard shells) — built from the traits' contributions.</div>
+     <div role="listitem"><i>style</i><b>Tokens &amp; brands</b>Every colour/size/type value once; compiled to CSS, TS, Tailwind, Swift, Kotlin; switched by brand + theme.</div>
+     <div role="listitem"><i>export + check</i><b>Tools</b>25 registered tools (19 auto + 6 on demand), as defined by <span class="k">packages/mcp-server/src/tools/registry.json</span>: compose, validate, render, code, charts, dashboards, certify, tokens, catalog.</div>
+   </div>
+   <p>Everything lives in one repository as plain files: traits and objects are YAML (<span class="k">traits/</span>, <span class="k">objects/</span>, <span class="k">domains/</span>), tokens are JSON (<span class="k">packages/tokens/src/tokens/</span>), components are packaged for React and Vue (<span class="k">packages/components-react/</span>, <span class="k">packages/components-vue/</span>) with shared styles (<span class="k">packages/component-styles/</span>), and the tools are a local server (<span class="k">packages/mcp-server/</span>). A <b>tool</b> is a typed function — name plus JSON in, JSON out — that you call over the Model Context Protocol from an AI assistant, over HTTP from a panel, or from the command line. Nothing requires a hosted service.</p>
+
+   <!-- 2 -->
+   <h2 id="traits"><span class="n">02</span>Traits — what one is, what it contains</h2>
+   <div class="def"><b>Trait</b><p>A single YAML file describing one capability an object can have — "has a lifecycle", "can be priced", "can be searched". The file carries everything that capability needs so that adding the trait to an object adds its data, its UI and its styling in one step.</p></div>
+   <p>A trait file has a header (<span class="k">trait:</span> name, version, category, description) and seven sections — plus two optional ones, <span class="k">actions</span> and <span class="k">state_machine</span>, that only chart traits use today. Using <span class="k">Stateful</span> (the lifecycle trait) as the example:</p>
+   <div class="tw"><table>
+     <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>What it declares</th><th>Stateful's actual content</th></tr></thead>
+     <tbody>
+       <tr><td>parameters</td><td>Settings the object sets when it uses the trait (typed, with defaults and validation).</td><td><span class="k">states</span> (ordered list), <span class="k">initialState</span> (must be one of states), <span class="k">transitionRules</span> (allowed from→to map; open when omitted), <span class="k">requireTransitionReason</span></td></tr>
+       <tr><td>schema</td><td>The data fields the trait adds to any object that uses it.</td><td><span class="k">status</span> (one of states), <span class="k">state_history</span> (from, to, timestamp, actor, reason), <span class="k">allowed_transitions</span> (computed next states)</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>semantics</td><td>What each field <em>means</em> (a semantic type), which token group styles it, and the default component for it. The screen composer uses this to pick a component for any field no view extension covers.</td><td>status → <span class="k">status.state</span> → StatusBadge · state_history → <span class="k">timeline.state_transition</span> → StatusTimeline · allowed_transitions → StatusSelector</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>view_extensions</td><td>Which UI piece to show in each context, where, and with what props.</td><td>list: StatusBadge · detail: StatusTimeline (top, priority 40) · form: StatusSelector · timeline: StateTransitionEvent · card: StatusBadge</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>tokens</td><td>The styling hooks those pieces use, pointing at system tokens. Merged into the object and carried into every rendered screen as token overrides.</td><td><span class="k">status.timeline.connector → var(--border-subtle)</span>, <span class="k">status.timeline.node.bg → var(--sys-surface-raised)</span> …</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>dependencies</td><td>Traits that must be present first.</td><td>none — but Archivable, Auditable, Cancellable and Colorized all depend on Stateful</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>metadata</td><td>Maturity, owners, accessibility notes (keyboard, screen reader), who composes it.</td><td>stable · "StatusSelector is keyboard-navigable (arrow keys, Enter)"</td></tr>
+     </tbody>
+   </table></div>
+   <p>The relevant part of the real file:</p>
+ <pre><code>trait:
+   name: Stateful
+   version: 2.0.0
+   category: lifecycle
+ parameters:
+   - name: states          <span class="cmt"># ordered list of valid states, e.g. draft → active → archived</span>
+     type: string[]
+   - name: initialState
+     validation: { enumFromParameter: states }
+   - name: transitionRules <span class="cmt"># { draft: [active, archived], active: [paused, archived], ... }</span>
+ schema:
+   status:            { type: string, validation: { enumFromParameter: states } }
+   state_history:     { type: StateTransition[] }   <span class="cmt"># from, to, timestamp, actor_id, reason</span>
+   allowed_transitions: { type: string[] }
+ view_extensions:
+   list:     [{ component: StatusBadge,          props: { field: status } }]
+   detail:   [{ component: StatusTimeline, position: top, priority: 40 }]
+   form:     [{ component: StatusSelector,       props: { optionsParameter: states } }]
+   timeline: [{ component: StateTransitionEvent, props: { historyField: state_history } }]
+ tokens:
+   status.timeline.connector: "var(--border-subtle)"</code></pre>
+   <h3>How a trait works once applied</h3>
+   <p>An object names the trait and sets its parameters — Product's file says:</p>
+ <pre><code>- name: lifecycle/Stateful
+   parameters: { states: [draft, in_review, active, retired], initialState: draft }</code></pre>
+   <p>From that, Product gains a <span class="k">status</span> field restricted to those four values, a transition history, and a computed list of next states; every Product list shows a status badge, every detail page a status timeline, every form a status selector whose options come from the object's own states. Parameters flow into component props (<span class="k">optionsParameter: states</span>), so the same StatusSelector is correct for Product's four states and Subscription's eight. Parameter values are checked against each trait's JSON Schema (<span class="k">schemas/traits/&lt;name&gt;.parameters.schema.json</span>) when the full engine resolves an object — <span class="k">pnpm object:validate</span>, <span class="k">object:compose</span>, <span class="k">object:generate</span>; the tools' lighter composer merges without validating, so run <span class="k">object:validate</span> after editing an object.</p>
+
+   <!-- 3 -->
+   <h2 id="trait-inventory"><span class="n">03</span>The trait inventory (41)</h2>
+   <p>What each trait adds, in plain terms. "Adds" lists the data fields; "Shows" lists the UI pieces it contributes. Maturity: stable unless marked. (If you only want the concepts, skip to section 04.)</p>
+   <div class="tw"><table class="fam">
+     <thead><tr><th>Trait</th><th>What it does</th><th>Adds</th><th>Shows</th></tr></thead>
+     <tbody>
+       <tr class="famrow"><td colspan="4">Lifecycle</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Stateful</td><td>Lifecycle states and governed transitions.</td><td>status, state_history, allowed_transitions</td><td>StatusBadge, StatusTimeline, StatusSelector, StateTransitionEvent</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Timestampable</td><td>Created/updated timestamps plus the last recorded event.</td><td>created_at, updated_at, last_event, last_event_at</td><td>RelativeTimestamp, AuditTimeline, AuditEvent</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Archivable</td><td>Archive → restore → purge with grace and retention windows (needs Stateful).</td><td>is_archived, archived_at, restored_at, archive_reason, archived_by</td><td>ArchivedRowOverlay, ArchiveSummary, ArchiveEvent, ArchivePill</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Cancellable</td><td>Cancellation workflow with windows and reason codes (needs Stateful).</td><td>cancel_at_period_end, cancellation_reason(_code), cancellation_requested_at</td><td>CancellationSummary, CancellationEvent, CancellationForm, CancellationBadge</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Auditable <small>(experimental)</small></td><td>Append-only audit log of state transitions with actor and reason (needs Stateful).</td><td>audit_log</td><td>AuditTimeline, AuditSummaryCard</td></tr>
+       <tr class="famrow"><td colspan="4">Behavioral</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Searchable</td><td>Full-text search box wired to query state.</td><td>searchQuery, searchActive</td><td>SearchInput</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Filterable</td><td>Multi-facet filter panel.</td><td>filters, activeFilters, filterCount</td><td>FilterPanel</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Sortable</td><td>Column sorting (ascending / descending / off).</td><td>sortField, sortDirection, sortActive</td><td>SortIndicator</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Pageable</td><td>Pagination with page-size options.</td><td>page, pageSize, totalItems, totalPages</td><td>PaginationBar</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Taggable</td><td>Tags — free-form or from an allowed list, optional moderation and synonyms.</td><td>tags, tag_count, tag_metadata</td><td>TagPills, TagManager, TagInput, TagSummary</td></tr>
+       <tr class="famrow"><td colspan="4">Content &amp; structure</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Labelled</td><td>Canonical label, description and placeholder text for every context.</td><td>label, description, placeholder</td><td>LabelCell, DetailHeader, FormLabelGroup, CardHeader, TimelineEntryLabel, InlineLabel</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Ownerable</td><td>Owner link (organization / team / user by default; objects override) with transfer audit.</td><td>owner_id, owner_type, ownership_role, ownership_transferred_at</td><td>OwnerBadge, OwnershipSummary, OwnershipMeta</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Classifiable <small>(draft)</small></td><td>Category tree, free tags, or both — with a tag policy (open / locked), a tag cap and an optional required primary category.</td><td>categories, primary_category_id/_path, tags, tag_count</td><td>ClassificationBadge, ClassificationPanel, ClassificationEditor</td></tr>
+       <tr class="famrow"><td colspan="4">Financial</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Priceable</td><td>Price with currency, pricing model, billing interval and tax behaviour.</td><td>unit_amount_cents, currency, pricing_model, billing_interval, tax_behavior</td><td>PriceBadge, PriceSummary, PriceCardMeta</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Billable <small>(experimental)</small></td><td>Recurring billing cycle: amount, interval, payment status, period progress, proration.</td><td>amount, currency, billing_interval, payment_status, current_period_start/end/progress, next_payment_due_at …</td><td>BillingSummaryBadge, CycleProgressCard, PaymentTimeline, PaymentEventTimeline, BillingIntervalSelector, BillingAmountInput, BillingCardMeta</td></tr>
+       <tr class="famrow"><td colspan="4">Core (experimental)</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Addressable</td><td>Addresses by role (billing, shipping, office…) with validation and geocoding hooks.</td><td>addresses, address_roles, default_address_role</td><td>AddressSummaryBadge, AddressCollectionPanel, AddressEditor, AddressValidationTimeline</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Authable</td><td>Role-based access: roles, permissions, memberships, role hierarchy.</td><td>role_catalog, permission_catalog, membership_records, role_hierarchy_edges …</td><td>RoleBadgeList, MembershipPanel, RoleAssignmentForm, MembershipAuditTimeline</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Preferenceable</td><td>Preferences by namespace (theme, notifications, display, privacy) with versioning.</td><td>preference_document, preference_version, preference_namespaces …</td><td>PreferenceSummaryBadge, PreferencePanel, PreferenceEditor, PreferenceTimeline</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Communicable</td><td>Multi-channel messaging: channels, templates, delivery policies, conversations (needs Preferenceable + Authable).</td><td>channel_catalog, template_catalog, delivery_policies, messages, conversations</td><td>MessageStatusBadge, CommunicationDetailPanel, TemplatePicker, MessageEventTimeline</td></tr>
+       <tr class="famrow"><td colspan="4">Visual</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Colorized</td><td>Maps lifecycle states to colour tokens (needs Stateful).</td><td>color_state, resolved_token_set, accessibility_label</td><td>ColorSwatch, StatusColorLegend, ColorStatePicker, ColorizedBadge</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>Statusable <small>(experimental)</small></td><td>Status registry: raw status strings → a tone (success / warning / danger / neutral) plus badge and banner tokens, per domain.</td><td>status, domain, tone, badge_tokens, banner_tokens</td><td>Badge, StatusBadge, Banner</td></tr>
+       <tr class="famrow"><td colspan="4">Charts (16, alpha/beta)</td></tr>
+       <tr><td>MarkBar · MarkLine · MarkArea · MarkPoint</td><td>The four chart mark types (bars, lines, areas, points) with their visual settings.</td><td>viz_mark_type, orientation / curve / shape …, viz_mark_a11y_label</td><td>Viz&lt;Mark&gt;Preview, Viz&lt;Mark&gt;Controls, VizRoleBadge</td></tr>
